{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c49f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb4-3612-7082-aba0-c5e534814a47"},"sequence":170,"recorded_at":1780531400000335,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50"},"call_id":"call_01a06fb5916873e38fc3ca71dc3a98e6","text":"Read text file `/tmp/r2verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1snnef review verdict — round 2\n2|\n3|**Verdict: changes requested → `to-dev`.**\n4|\n5|CR `CR-TASK-260830-1snnef-2` rev 2, base `57afcc6`, candidate tree\n6|`4400b106c826536d499d8e13a871c41af9764daa`. I verified the tree I measured **is**\n7|the candidate: a scratch-index `git write-tree` returned `4400b106…` before the\n8|first probe and again after the last one, every mutation restored.\n9|\n10|Round 1's four findings are **closed for real** — I killed each one with my own\n11|mutants, not by reading the rework note. The Story's four inherited batteries\n12|re-measure identically, zero resurrections. The two closed derivation shapes stay\n13|closed under replay.\n14|\n15|Three findings block, all one family and all cheap: **a bounded, enumerable domain\n16|measured by a sample and stated as a closure.** That is the class that blocked\n17|round 1 (F2); this round it sits on three surfaces, one of which is the third\n18|derivation shape the brief asked me to hunt.\n19|\n20|---\n21|\n22|## Round-1 findings: verified closed, by attack\n23|\n24|| Round-1 finding | My mutant | Result |\n25|| --- | --- | --- |\n26|| F1 shape A (`var f = func() *Error`) | W4: package-level `var plantedRefusal = &Error{…}` returned from a `switch` | **RED** — both bijection directions |\n27|| F1 shape B (`refuse := mismatchf`) | W2b/W2c: parametric wrapper `refuseFrame(detail)` → `integrityFailure(detail)` | **RED** — both directions |\n28|| F2 (`CheckErrorAllowed` sample) | C01: admit `terminal_backend_unavailable` for all ten operations | **RED** — `TestCheckErrorAllowedRefusesEveryUnlistedCode` |\n29|| F3 (triple equality third leg) | C02: drop the `auth.InputAuthorized` conjunct | **RED** — `TestCheckAttachResultRequiresTripleEquality` |\n30|| F4 (expiry boundary instant) | C03: `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` | **RED** — `TestCheckAttachRequestBindsTransportInputAndExpiry` |\n31|\n32|F2's rebuild is the right shape: the complement derives from\n33|`catalog.Current().Errors`, the mirror is pinned inside the catalog, and the\n34|zero-catalog floor fails closed. The admit direction proves mirror ⊆ production and\n35|the complement direction proves production ⊆ mirror over the pinned vocabulary — a\n36|real bijection, not a closed loop.\n37|\n38|**Correction in the producer's favour:** round-1's declared survivor **P11** is no\n39|longer a survivor. C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\"screen\": BuiltinTmux`) is **RED**,\n40|killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`. The \"declined closure\"\n41|bound for P11 in LOGBOOK 0022 is stale — the closed-set property is pinned.\n42|\n43|---\n44|\n45|## G-A — the ratio, and the third shape\n46|\n47|### Denominator, built three ways independent of the derivation under test\n48|\n49|| Method | What it counts | Result |\n50|| --- | --- | ---: |\n51|| Whole-file `ast.Inspect`, positional exclusion of the two constructor bodies | `&Error{}` literals + direct `mismatchf`/`integrityFailure` calls | 75 + 118 = **193** |\n52|| Constructor identifier accounting | 120 idents = 118 call-funs + 2 decl names | **residual 0** |\n53|| Declared table + funnel (the suite's own green bijection) | 192 rows + 1 | **193** |\n54|\n55|**193 of 193 arms derived and declared — 100%.** New this round, and the reason I\n56|can say the two closed shapes are still *empty* rather than merely *handled*:\n57|`outsideAnyFuncDecl = 0`, `insideVarInitializer = 0`, `residual alias refs = 0`, and\n58|a census of single-return refusal wrappers returns **0 candidates** — no\n59|`refuseFrame`-style funnel exists in the tree at all.\n60|\n61|### Attacks on the arm derivation: 10 of 10 killed or fail-closed\n62|\n63|| # | Shape | Result |\n64|| --- | --- | --- |\n65|| W1 | one-line wrapper `refuseFrame() → mismatchf(\"literal\")`, called from `CheckReplicable` | RED |\n66|| W2b | parametric wrapper → `integrityFailure(detail)`, caller passes a new literal | RED (both directions) |\n67|| W2c | same wrapper, caller passes an **already-declared** detail | RED (function key) |\n68|| W3 | wrapper returning `&Error{Detail: detail}` with a parameterised detail | RED |\n69|| W4 | package-level `var` holding a prebuilt refusal, returned from a `switch` | RED |\n70|| W6 | refusal on a method of a new type, reached via a package-level **method value** | RED |\n71|| W7 | arm in a **new build-tagged** production file (`//go:build darwin`) | RED |\n72|| W8 | arm in a new file **excluded from this build** (`//go:build linux`) | RED |\n73|| W17 | arm in a nested func literal inside a `FuncDecl` (re-verify A4) | RED |\n74|| W14b | delete an existing arm (reverse-direction control) | RED |\n75|\n76|Note: `mismatchf` is variadic-format, so `go vet`'s printf analyzer refuses a\n77|non-constant format string — the `mismatchf(detail)` variant dies at the compiler,\n78|not at the inventory. Worth knowing which guard is actually holding that line.\n79|\n80|### The third shape is on the *sibling* guard in the same file\n81|\n82|`TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walks `file.Decls` → `*ast.FuncDecl`\n83|bodies **only** — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1,\n84|200 lines above it, left unextended here.\n85|\n86|| # | Shape | Result |\n87|| --- | --- | --- |\n88|| W15 | **CONTROL** — `errors.New(\"planted plain refusal\")` inside a `FuncDecl` body | **RED** |\n89|| W5b | the **same string**, in a package-level `var errPlanted = errors.New(…)`, returned from `validateProtocolVersions` | **GREEN** |\n90|| W9b | same, `fmt.Errorf` | **GREEN** |\n91|| W16 | plain error inside a package-level `var f = func() error { … }` | **GREEN** |\n92|| W12 | `errors.New` in a **new** production file's `FuncDecl` | RED |\n93|\n94|Identical text, identical production reachability, opposite verdicts, decided purely\n95|by declaration position. **2 of 6 plain-error attacks killed.**\n96|\n97|The file's claim is a closure claim, in its own words:\n98|\n99|> `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` closes the smuggling hole: a non-wire\n100|> error constructed **anywhere** but validatePlatforms … or DigestFile … fails, so a\n101|> refusal wearing a plain error's clothes **cannot ship unwitnessed**.\n102|\n103|W5b ships one and the suite stays green, with `gofmt`, `go vet` and all 14 packages\n104|clean. The \"Stated bounds\" block asserts the same property (\"They live only in\n105|validatePlatforms … and DigestFile … Both properties are asserted below\").\n106|\n107|Severity is below round-1's F1 — a plain error carries no wire code, so this is not\n108|a forged wire refusal — but it is the failure this file exists to prevent, for the\n109|half of it that plain errors own.\n110|\n111|**Fix: the same ~12-line `GenDecl`/`ValueSpec` loop already written above it**, so\n112|one walk covers both guards.\n113|\n114|---\n115|\n116|## G-B — the whole Story, re-measured\n117|\n118|Production files are **byte-identical** between rev 1 and rev 2 (`manifest.go`,\n119|`terminalbackend.go`, `conformance.go`, `internal/config/validation.go` all hash\n120|equal), so every battery result below measures the *test* delta.\n121|\n122|| Battery | Applied | Killed | Survived | Anchor missing | vs round 1 |\n123|| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n124|| Leaf 1 review-3 (71) | 70 | 61 | 9 | 1 (N12) | **identical** |\n125|| Leaf 1 review-2 (60) | 59 | 54 | 5 | 1 (N12) | **identical** |\n126|| Leaf 2 battery-1 (60) | 58 | 58 | **0** | 2 | **identical** |\n127|| Leaf 2 battery-2 (47) | 47 | 47 | **0** | 0 | **identical** |\n128|\n129|**Zero resurrections.** Survivor sets reproduce element for element\n130|(N09/N13/N14/N15/T01/X01/X02/X04/X10 and N09/N13/N14/N15/T01).\n131|\n132|**T01 re-verified directly.** I applied the self-minted-declaration mutant to\n133|`ownership.v0.5.0.json` and ran the traceability packages: **KILLED**, eleven tests\n134|red including\n135|`TestVerifyRepositoryRejectsForgedOwnershipAndCapabilityClaims/valid_declaration_cannot_self-mint_ownership`.\n136|This leaf's `+116`-line ownership delta has not weakened that gate.\n137|\n138|Note for whoever runs these next: the battery runner restores only the four Go\n139|files, so a T01 run leaves `ownership.v0.5.0.json` mutated. I caught it against the\n140|tree OID and restored it; the candidate carries no residue from round 1 either.\n141|\n142|---\n143|\n144|## This leaf's own delta — my battery, 46 mutants\n145|\n146|The P-series from round 1 was the reviewer's; I built my own, larger and\n147|independent. **Every mutant preserves every refusal literal**, so the arm inventory\n148|cannot kill any of them by construction — the kill-inflation bound is neutralised by\n149|design and only behavioural tests can score.\n150|\n151|**34 of 46 killed (74%). 12 survivors, in four clusters.**\n152|\n153|Killed, worth naming because they are the AC surfaces: C01 error-mapping widening;\n154|C02/C03/C04/C05/C06 the four attach-authorization conjuncts and the relay refusal;\n155|C07/C08b/C09 the `ax pane` entrypoint (argv shape, argv[0], session binding);\n156|C10/C11/C12 idempotency key shape and arity; C14/C15 status provider observation and\n157|the canonical false form; C16 replication class; C17 ledger rebind conflict;\n158|C18/C19 ledger image duplicate key and empty result; C20 legacy escape name;\n159|C21/C24 transition create resolution and instance scope; C22/C23 attach policy exact\n160|members and issue/expiry order; C25 legacy reverse projection grammar; C34–C39 six\n161|transition-table widenings (sources, effects, target); C40b/C40d two replication\n162|reclassifications.\n163|\n164|### G1 (blocking) — attachability is a two-state rule measured at one excluded state\n165|\n166|`CheckStatusResult`, `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go:770`:\n167|\n168|```go\n169|if result.Attachable && !((result.State == StateParked || result.State == StateActive) && result.AttachEvidenced) {\n170|```\n171|\n172|The instance-state domain is a **closed eight-value enum** that `ParseInstanceState`\n173|pins. The rule admits two. `TestCheckStatusResultEnforcesLookupRules` drives exactly\n174|**one** of the six excluded states:\n175|\n176|```go\n177|stopped := matched\n178|stopped.State = \"stopped\"\n179|```\n180|\n181|under the comment \"attachable **outside parked/active** … is refused\". Widening the\n182|state set one member at a time:\n183|\n184|| Mutant | Widened with | Result |\n185|| --- | --- | --- |\n186|| C30 | `StateStopped` | RED |\n187|| C13 | `StateQuiescing` | **GREEN** |\n188|| C26 | `StateCreating` | **GREEN** |\n189|| C27 | `StateAbsent` | **GREEN** |\n190|| C28 | `StateUnavailable` | **GREEN** |\n191|| C29 | `StateStaleFenced` | **GREEN** |\n192|\n193|**5 of 6 survive.** This is F2's shape on a domain that is not merely enumerable but\n194|already enumerated in the same file, on the §4.C attach/status surface the AC names.\n195|The fix is a loop over the eight states — three lines — and it closes the class\n196|instead of adding a seventh sample.\n197|\n198|### G2 (blocking) — the plain-error smuggling gate\n199|\n200|W5b/W9b/W16 survive against the W15 control; detail in G-A above. Same file, same\n201|fix already written 200 lines up.\n202|\n203|### G3 (blocking) — the replication table has no reverse direction\n204|\n205|`TestReplicationClassificationIsClosed` iterates its `want` map against production,\n206|which proves **want ⊆ production**. Nothing proves production ⊆ want, and nothing\n207|pins the table size.\n208|\n209|| Mutant | Result |\n210|| --- | --- |\n211|| C40b — reclassify the existing `native_pid` from forbidden to safe evidence | RED |\n212|| C40d — promote `attach_credential` from sensitive to safe evidence | RED |\n213|| C40c — **add** `\"ax_pane_pid\"` to the safe-evidence list | **GREEN** |\n214|| C40 — same, injected via `init()` | **GREEN** |\n215|\n216|A member the reviewed table never listed becomes replicable and the suite stays\n217|green. The doc comment says the test \"pins the whole §4.E table\"; it pins the half it\n218|iterates. The unknown-member probe is a four-string sample\n219|(`\"\", \"session_record\", \"MANIFEST_ID\", \"manifest_id \"`).\n220|\n221|\"Replication exclusions\" is named in the AC verbatim. The opening paragraph of\n222|`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` diagnoses this exact failure mode for arms — \"the\n223|forward direction alone passes vacuously\" — and the replication table is the same\n224|shape without the second direction. A size pin from an internal test, or an AST\n225|derivation in the file's own idiom, closes it.\n226|\n227|### G4 (not blocking, but it must stop being stated as a closure)\n228|\n229|Three vocabulary tests are named and commented as sweeps and are samples:\n230|\n231|| Mutant | Result |\n232|| --- | --- |\n233|| C31 — `ParseInstanceState` admits `\"running\"` | RED (in the refused sample) |\n234|| C44 — `ParseInstanceState` admits `\"detached\"` | **GREEN** |\n235|| C32 — `ParseOperation` admits `\"detach\"` | **GREEN** |\n236|| C43 — `ParseSideEffect` admits `\"input_reopened\"` | **GREEN** |\n237|| C33 — `parseTransport` admits `\"ssh_tunnel\"` | **GREEN** |\n238|\n239|C31 and C44 are the same mutation on the same test with a different string. The\n240|domain is unbounded, so by round 1's own standard (P11) this is a **bound to\n241|report**, not a blocker — except that it is currently stated as a closure three times\n242|(`…AdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations`; \"sweeps the operation domain the same way: no\n243|eleventh operation is admittable\"), **and** the F2 rework cites one of them as its\n244|pin:\n245|\n246|> `conformanceOperations` … matching the ten operations ParseOperation admits\n247|> (pinned by `TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations`).\n248|\n249|That citation does not hold. Either close it by AST derivation over the `switch` case\n250|list — the repo's own idiom, the one `deriveRefusalArms` and\n251|`grammar_inventory_test.go` already use — or restate all three as sampling bounds and\n252|drop the \"pinned by\" clause.\n253|\n254|### Bounds I am not blocking on, to be recorded\n255|\n256|- **W11** — a new `errors.New` inside `DigestFile` survives. The allowlist is\n257|  function-wide with no detail pin, unlike `validatePlatforms`, whose funneled detail\n258|  set is derived and exact. Asymmetric; disclose or mirror.\n259|- **W13** — a custom error type (`type plantedErr struct{}`) smuggled as a refusal\n260|  survives: neither `*Error` nor one of the two recognised plain-error spellings.\n261|  \"A non-wire error constructed anywhere\" does not cover it.\n262|- **C45** — `allowedOperationErrors` widened with a **non-catalogued** code\n263|  (`\"terminal_backend_smuggled\"`) survives. Already disclosed in-test as the\n264|  unbounded-domain bound. **No action needed** — this is the honest version of G4.\n265|- `mismatchf` is `func(format string, arguments ...any)`. A `mismatchf(\"x %s\", v)`\n266|  site would be inventoried under its format string while interpolating local data,\n267|  which the constructor's own comment forbids. Zero such sites today (measured: all\n268|  118 calls pass exactly one string literal); `go vet` catches the non-constant case.\n269|  One assertion or one bound line.\n270|\n271|---\n272|\n273|## G-C — the bounds, and whether they reached the tree\n274|\n275|Both round-1 bounds are **in the tree**, not only on the board:\n276|\n277|| Bound | Where |\n278|| --- | --- |\n279|| Kill inflation — the inventory fails on any added/deleted arm, so post-leaf-3 scores are **not comparable** to leaf 2's 91/95; review the failing-test list, not the exit code | `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` \"Stated bounds\" block, lines 34–40, **and** LOGBOOK |\n280|| Attribution drift via the entry+code fallback, with `CheckTransition`'s dead `\"operation vocabulary\"` arm as the live example and the five re-parse arms as the contrast | same block, lines 25–33, **and** LOGBOOK |\n281|\n282|Coverage figure corrected: LOGBOOK now records 89.9% on the rev-1 tree as my\n283|predecessor measured it and 90.0% on this one. **I measure 90.0% on this tree.**\n284|Accurate.\n285|\n286|## Gates I ran myself\n287|\n288|| Gate | Result |\n289|| --- | --- |\n290|| `go test ./... -count=1` | **exit 0**, 14/14 packages ok |\n291|| `go test ./internal/terminalbackend/ -race -count=1` | **exit 0** |\n292|| `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n293|| `gofmt -l .` | clean |\n294|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | exit 0, `acceptance_cases=76`, `bindings=49 … clauses_discharged=17/403` |\n295|| `go test ./internal/terminalbackend/ -cover` | **90.0%** |\n296|| Candidate tree identity, before first probe and after last | `4400b106c826536d499d8e13a871c41af9764daa` ✓ |\n297|\n298|Architecture fit is unchanged and good: the harness holds no authority, does no I/O,\n299|leaves capability gating in `manifest.go` and trust in `terminalbackend.go`. The\n300|stated bound from round 1 still applies — nothing outside `internal/terminalbackend`\n301|calls these entry points, by design per §4.B, so \"production entry point\" here means\n302|the harness's own exported surface.\n303|\n304|---\n305|\n306|## What acceptance needs\n307|\n308|1. **G1** — derive the attachability refusal over all eight states instead of\n309|   sampling `stopped`. Kill C13/C26/C27/C28/C29.\n310|2. **G2** — extend `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` past `FuncDecl`\n311|   bodies (the `GenDecl`/`ValueSpec` loop already in this file). Kill W5b/W9b/W16 and\n312|   keep W15 red.\n313|3. **G3** — give the replication table its reverse direction, or pin its size. Kill\n314|   C40c.\n315|4. **G4** — close the three vocabulary sweeps by derivation, or restate them as\n316|   sampling bounds **and** drop the \"pinned by\n317|   `TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations`\" citation from\n318|   `conformanceOperations`.\n319|5. Record W11, W13 and the `mismatchf` format-verb note as bounds. Drop or restate the\n320|   now-stale P11 \"declined closure\" bound — C20 is killed.\n321|6. Report the conformance survivor set as a ratio, including anything declined.\n322|\n323|Everything from round 1 is genuinely closed and the Story's other two leaves\n324|re-measure clean against this tree. These four are the same family, on surfaces the\n325|AC names, and each is a few lines. Once they land, this leaf is ready.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
