{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb4-3612-7082-aba0-c5e534814a47"},"sequence":249,"recorded_at":1780531400000493,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a9f280dd-3b8e-45be-b479-8bde8ee013b6"},"task_id":"a9f280dd-3b8e-45be-b479-8bde8ee013b6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a9f280dd-3b8e-45be-b479-8bde8ee013b6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|// AST-derived refusal-arm inventory for the terminal backend packages.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a brand-new production refusal\n4|// arm carrying a brand-new unasserted detail shipped while `gofmt`,\n5|// `go vet`, `go test ./...`, and `tracecheck` all stayed green. A\n6|// hand-maintained arm list cannot catch that; a derived one can, but only\n7|// if it is checked in BOTH directions. The forward direction alone passes\n8|// vacuously on a truncated derivation: every derived arm asserted is true\n9|// when the derivation silently dropped half the package. So this file\n10|// derives every refusal arm from the production AST, requires each to\n11|// resolve to exactly one declared row naming a real asserting test, and\n12|// requires every declared row to resolve to exactly one derived arm.\n13|//\n14|// Modelled on internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go: derivation\n15|// fails closed on an empty, short, or unparseable input, and the declared\n16|// table cannot move its own goalposts because the derivation never\n17|// consults it.\n18|//\n19|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n20|//   - The inventory proves every arm is DECLARED with a resolving test.\n21|//     Execution and decision proof is each row's named test, measured by\n22|//     this package's suite. A row resolves textually (detail mention, or\n23|//     entry-plus-code/predicate mention); a wrongly attributed row that\n24|//     still resolves is a review finding, not a green light.\n25|//   - Attribution drift survives through that fallback: a\n26|//     dead-by-construction arm can resolve through a sibling site's test\n27|//     while pointing at the wrong guard. Live example: CheckTransition's\n28|//     \"operation vocabulary\" arm (conformance.go) is unreachable —\n29|//     ParseOperation admits exactly the ten operations transitionTable\n30|//     covers, so lookupTransition never misses — yet the row carries no\n31|//     bound and resolves through TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations,\n32|//     which drives ParseOperation's own arm sharing the detail. The five\n33|//     re-parse arms are the contrast: they declare boundDefensiveReparse\n34|//     and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n35|//   - Kill inflation: both inventory directions fail on ANY added or\n36|//     deleted production arm by construction, so an arm-deleting mutant\n37|//     elsewhere reads as killed by the inventory alone with no behavioral\n38|//     change. Mutation scores measured with this file present are NOT\n39|//     comparable to pre-inventory scores; review the failing-test list,\n40|//     not just the exit code.\n41|//   - errors.New/fmt.Errorf sites are not wire refusals and carry no arm.\n42|//     They live only in validatePlatforms (funneled into one *Error arm\n43|//     whose detail set is pinned exactly) and DigestFile (I/O errors that\n44|//     must never be *Error). Both properties are asserted below.\n45|package terminalbackend\n46|\n47|import (\n48|\t\"errors\"\n49|\t\"go/ast\"\n50|\t\"go/parser\"\n51|\t\"go/token\"\n52|\t\"os\"\n53|\t\"path/filepath\"\n54|\t\"strconv\"\n55|\t\"strings\"\n56|\t\"testing\"\n57|)\n58|\n59|// refusalArm is one derived production refusal: a wire-code *Error\n60|// construction site keyed by file, enclosing function (receiver-qualified\n61|// for methods), code symbol, static detail, and occurrence index within\n62|// that key. The index keeps two identical arms in one function distinct:\n63|// adding a second arm with an already-declared key fails on the missing\n64|// #2 row instead of hiding behind #1.\n65|type refusalArm struct {\n66|\tfile       string\n67|\tfunction   string\n68|\tcode       string\n69|\tdetail     string\n70|\toccurrence int\n71|}\n72|\n73|// constructorFunctions build refusals instead of issuing them. Their own\n74|// *Error sites are the funnel, not arms.\n75|var constructorFunctions = map[string]bool{\n76|\t\"mismatchf\":        true,\n77|\t\"integrityFailure\": true,\n78|}\n79|\n80|// passthroughDetail marks the single dynamic-detail funnel: Registration\n81|// validation wraps validatePlatforms errors via err.Error(). Every other\n82|// Detail expression must be a static string literal; a new dynamic detail\n83|// fails the derivation rather than entering the table silently.\n84|const passthroughDetail = \"passthrough:err.Error()\"\n85|\n86|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n87|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n88|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n89|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n90|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n91|//\n92|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n93|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n94|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n95|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n96|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n97|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n98|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n99|// than shipping silently.\n100|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n101|\tt.Helper()\n102|\n103|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n104|\tif err != nil {\n105|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n106|\t}\n107|\tvar production []string\n108|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n109|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n110|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n111|\t\t}\n112|\t}\n113|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n114|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n115|\t}\n116|\n117|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n118|\tparsed := 0\n119|\tfor _, name := range production {\n120|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n121|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n122|\t\tif err != nil {\n123|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n124|\t\t}\n125|\t\tparsed++\n126|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n127|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n128|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n129|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n130|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n131|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n132|\t\t\t\t\t}\n133|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n134|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n135|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n136|\t\t\t\t\t}\n137|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n138|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n139|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n140|\t\t\t\t\t}\n141|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n142|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n143|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n144|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n145|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n146|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n147|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n148|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n149|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n150|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n151|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n152|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n153|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n154|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n155|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n156|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n157|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n159|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n162|\t\t\t\t\t}\n163|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n166|\t\t\t\t\t}\n167|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n169|\t\t\t\t\t})\n170|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n171|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n172|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n174|\t\t\t\t\t}\n175|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) == 0 {\n176|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s without arguments; the derivation cannot name its detail\",\n177|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name)\n178|\t\t\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n180|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n181|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n183|\t\t\t\t\t}\n184|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n185|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n187|\t\t\t\t\t}\n188|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n191|\t\t\t\t\t}\n192|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n194|\t\t\t\t\t})\n195|\t\t\t\t}\n196|\t\t\t\treturn true\n197|\t\t\t})\n198|\t\t}\n199|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n200|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n201|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n202|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n203|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n204|\t\t\t\t}\n205|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n206|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n207|\t\t\t\t}\n208|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n209|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n210|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n211|\t\t\t\t}\n212|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n213|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n214|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n215|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n216|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n217|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n218|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n219|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n220|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n221|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n222|\t\t\t\t\t}\n223|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n224|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n225|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n226|\t\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n228|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n229|\t\t\t\t\t}\n230|\t\t\t\t}\n231|\t\t\t}\n232|\t\t}\n233|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n234|\t}\n235|\t_ = parsed\n236|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n237|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n238|\t}\n239|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n240|\tfor index := range arms {\n241|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n242|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n243|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n244|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n245|\t}\n246|\treturn arms\n247|}\n248|\n249|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n250|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n251|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n252|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n253|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n254|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n255|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n256|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n257|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n258|\tt.Helper()\n259|\n260|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n261|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n262|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n263|\t\tif !ok {\n264|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n265|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n266|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n267|\t\t\t\t}\n268|\t\t\t}\n269|\t\t\treturn true\n270|\t\t}\n271|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n272|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n273|\t\t\treturn false\n274|\t\t}\n275|\t\treturn true\n276|\t})\n277|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n278|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n279|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n280|\t\t\treturn false\n281|\t\t}\n282|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n283|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n284|\t\t\treturn true\n285|\t\t}\n286|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n287|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n288|\t\treturn true\n289|\t})\n290|}\n291|\n292|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n293|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n294|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n295|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n296|\t\treturn typed.Name\n297|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n298|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n299|\tdefault:\n300|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n301|\t}\n302|}\n303|\n304|// staticDetail reads one Detail expression: a string literal, or the one\n305|// dynamic funnel. Anything else fails the derivation.\n306|func staticDetail(t *testing.T, function string, expression ast.Expr) string {\n307|\tt.Helper()\n308|\n309|\tif literal, ok := expression.(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n310|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n311|\t\tif err != nil {\n312|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", function, err)\n313|\t\t}\n314|\t\treturn detail\n315|\t}\n316|\tif call, ok := expression.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n317|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok && selector.Sel.Name == \"Error\" {\n318|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok && receiver.Name == \"err\" {\n319|\t\t\t\treturn passthroughDetail\n320|\t\t\t}\n321|\t\t}\n322|\t}\n323|\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal Detail is not a static clause; Detail must never \"+\n324|\t\t\"interpolate local data, and a dynamic detail cannot be inventoried\", function)\n325|\treturn \"\"\n326|}\n327|\n328|// productionCodeSymbols resolves every Code symbol to its wire value from\n329|// the production const declarations, so the declared table cannot drift\n330|// from the codes production actually emits.\n331|func productionCodeSymbols(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n332|\tt.Helper()\n333|\n334|\tsymbols := make(map[string]string)\n335|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n336|\tif err != nil {\n337|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n338|\t}\n339|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n340|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n341|\t\t\tcontinue\n342|\t\t}\n343|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n344|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n345|\t\tif err != nil {\n346|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n347|\t\t}\n348|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n349|\t\t\tgeneral, ok := declaration.(*ast.GenDecl)\n350|\t\t\tif !ok || general.Tok != token.CONST {\n351|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n352|\t\t\t}\n353|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range general.Specs {\n354|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n355|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n356|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n357|\t\t\t\t}\n358|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n359|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n360|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n361|\t\t\t\t\t}\n362|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n363|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n364|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n365|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n366|\t\t\t\t\t}\n367|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n368|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n369|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n370|\t\t\t\t\t}\n371|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n372|\t\t\t\t}\n373|\t\t\t}\n374|\t\t}\n375|\t}\n376|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n377|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n378|\t}\n379|\treturn symbols\n380|}\n381|\n382|// testBodies indexes every test declaration in this package by file and\n383|// name to its body source. A duplicate test name across files fails: row\n384|// references would be ambiguous.\n385|func testBodies(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n386|\tt.Helper()\n387|\n388|\tbodies := make(map[string]string)\n389|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*_test.go\")\n390|\tif err != nil {\n391|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob test files: %v\", err)\n392|\t}\n393|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n394|\t\tt.Fatal(\"found zero test files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n395|\t}\n396|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n397|\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(name)\n398|\t\tif err != nil {\n399|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n400|\t\t}\n401|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n402|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n403|\t\tif err != nil {\n404|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n405|\t\t}\n406|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n407|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n408|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Test\") {\n409|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n410|\t\t\t}\n411|\t\t\tstart := fileSet.Position(function.Body.Pos()).Offset\n412|\t\t\tend := fileSet.Position(function.Body.End()).Offset\n413|\t\t\tkey := name + \"\\n\" + function.Name.Name\n414|\t\t\tif _, duplicate := bodies[key]; duplicate {\n415|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"test %s is declared twice; row references would be ambiguous\", key)\n416|\t\t\t}\n417|\t\t\tbodies[key] = string(raw[start:end])\n418|\t\t}\n419|\t}\n420|\tif len(bodies) == 0 {\n421|\t\tt.Fatal(\"indexed zero test declarations, so every row below would resolve vacuously\")\n422|\t}\n423|\treturn bodies\n424|}\n425|\n426|// predicateCodes resolves every Is predicate to the code symbol it\n427|// reports, verifying the shape: a single return of errorCode(err, Code).\n428|// A predicate in any other shape fails: the inventory leans on these to\n429|// resolve code-only assertions, so an unrecognized shape proves nothing.\n430|func predicateCodes(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n431|\tt.Helper()\n432|\n433|\tpredicates := make(map[string]string)\n434|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n435|\tif err != nil {\n436|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n437|\t}\n438|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n439|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n440|\t\t\tcontinue\n441|\t\t}\n442|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n443|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n444|\t\tif err != nil {\n445|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n446|\t\t}\n447|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n448|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n449|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Is\") || function.Body == nil {\n450|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb4-3612-7082-aba0-c5e534814a47"},"sequence":250,"recorded_at":1780531400000495,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a9f280dd-3b8e-45be-b479-8bde8ee013b6"},"task_id":"a9f280dd-3b8e-45be-b479-8bde8ee013b6","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"a9f280dd-3b8e-45be-b479-8bde8ee013b6"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c541","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb4-3612-7082-aba0-c5e534814a47"},"sequence":251,"recorded_at":1780531400000497,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50"},"call_id":"call_01a06fb5c0447a929579d69edfd2801b","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|// AST-derived refusal-arm inventory for the terminal backend packages.\n2|//\n3|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a brand-new production refusal\n4|// arm carrying a brand-new unasserted detail shipped while `gofmt`,\n5|// `go vet`, `go test ./...`, and `tracecheck` all stayed green. A\n6|// hand-maintained arm list cannot catch that; a derived one can, but only\n7|// if it is checked in BOTH directions. The forward direction alone passes\n8|// vacuously on a truncated derivation: every derived arm asserted is true\n9|// when the derivation silently dropped half the package. So this file\n10|// derives every refusal arm from the production AST, requires each to\n11|// resolve to exactly one declared row naming a real asserting test, and\n12|// requires every declared row to resolve to exactly one derived arm.\n13|//\n14|// Modelled on internal/canonicaljson/grammar_inventory_test.go: derivation\n15|// fails closed on an empty, short, or unparseable input, and the declared\n16|// table cannot move its own goalposts because the derivation never\n17|// consults it.\n18|//\n19|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n20|//   - The inventory proves every arm is DECLARED with a resolving test.\n21|//     Execution and decision proof is each row's named test, measured by\n22|//     this package's suite. A row resolves textually (detail mention, or\n23|//     entry-plus-code/predicate mention); a wrongly attributed row that\n24|//     still resolves is a review finding, not a green light.\n25|//   - Attribution drift survives through that fallback: a\n26|//     dead-by-construction arm can resolve through a sibling site's test\n27|//     while pointing at the wrong guard. Live example: CheckTransition's\n28|//     \"operation vocabulary\" arm (conformance.go) is unreachable —\n29|//     ParseOperation admits exactly the ten operations transitionTable\n30|//     covers, so lookupTransition never misses — yet the row carries no\n31|//     bound and resolves through TestParseOperationAdmitsOnlyTheTenClosedOperations,\n32|//     which drives ParseOperation's own arm sharing the detail. The five\n33|//     re-parse arms are the contrast: they declare boundDefensiveReparse\n34|//     and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n35|//   - Kill inflation: both inventory directions fail on ANY added or\n36|//     deleted production arm by construction, so an arm-deleting mutant\n37|//     elsewhere reads as killed by the inventory alone with no behavioral\n38|//     change. Mutation scores measured with this file present are NOT\n39|//     comparable to pre-inventory scores; review the failing-test list,\n40|//     not just the exit code.\n41|//   - errors.New/fmt.Errorf sites are not wire refusals and carry no arm.\n42|//     They live only in validatePlatforms (funneled into one *Error arm\n43|//     whose detail set is pinned exactly) and DigestFile (I/O errors that\n44|//     must never be *Error). Both properties are asserted below.\n45|package terminalbackend\n46|\n47|import (\n48|\t\"errors\"\n49|\t\"go/ast\"\n50|\t\"go/parser\"\n51|\t\"go/token\"\n52|\t\"os\"\n53|\t\"path/filepath\"\n54|\t\"strconv\"\n55|\t\"strings\"\n56|\t\"testing\"\n57|)\n58|\n59|// refusalArm is one derived production refusal: a wire-code *Error\n60|// construction site keyed by file, enclosing function (receiver-qualified\n61|// for methods), code symbol, static detail, and occurrence index within\n62|// that key. The index keeps two identical arms in one function distinct:\n63|// adding a second arm with an already-declared key fails on the missing\n64|// #2 row instead of hiding behind #1.\n65|type refusalArm struct {\n66|\tfile       string\n67|\tfunction   string\n68|\tcode       string\n69|\tdetail     string\n70|\toccurrence int\n71|}\n72|\n73|// constructorFunctions build refusals instead of issuing them. Their own\n74|// *Error sites are the funnel, not arms.\n75|var constructorFunctions = map[string]bool{\n76|\t\"mismatchf\":        true,\n77|\t\"integrityFailure\": true,\n78|}\n79|\n80|// passthroughDetail marks the single dynamic-detail funnel: Registration\n81|// validation wraps validatePlatforms errors via err.Error(). Every other\n82|// Detail expression must be a static string literal; a new dynamic detail\n83|// fails the derivation rather than entering the table silently.\n84|const passthroughDetail = \"passthrough:err.Error()\"\n85|\n86|// deriveRefusalArms walks every production file of this package (every\n87|// *.go except *_test.go, so a new production file is scanned without\n88|// anyone remembering it) and returns every refusal arm in source order.\n89|// It fails closed: an unparseable file, a non-static code or detail, and\n90|// an empty result are all fatal, never an empty table.\n91|//\n92|// Coverage is declaration-complete, not FuncDecl-complete: every FuncDecl\n93|// body (including nested func literals, methods, and init) plus every\n94|// package-level var initializer is scanned, so a refusal arm hiding in a\n95|// package-level `var f = func() *Error {...}` is derived like any other.\n96|// Constructor references outside direct-call position (`refuse :=\n97|// mismatchf`) are rejected outright by rejectConstructorAliases below:\n98|// an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, so it fails the suite rather\n99|// than shipping silently.\n100|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n101|\tt.Helper()\n102|\n103|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n104|\tif err != nil {\n105|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n106|\t}\n107|\tvar production []string\n108|\tfor _, match := range matches {\n109|\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(match, \"_test.go\") {\n110|\t\t\tproduction = append(production, match)\n111|\t\t}\n112|\t}\n113|\tif len(production) == 0 {\n114|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n115|\t}\n116|\n117|\tvar arms []refusalArm\n118|\tparsed := 0\n119|\tfor _, name := range production {\n120|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n121|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n122|\t\tif err != nil {\n123|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v; an unparseable derivation proves nothing\", name, err)\n124|\t\t}\n125|\t\tparsed++\n126|\t\tcollect := func(functionName string, root ast.Node) {\n127|\t\t\tast.Inspect(root, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n128|\t\t\t\tswitch expression := node.(type) {\n129|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.UnaryExpr:\n130|\t\t\t\t\tif expression.Op != token.AND {\n131|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n132|\t\t\t\t\t}\n133|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.X.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n134|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n135|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n136|\t\t\t\t\t}\n137|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n138|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || identifier.Name != \"Error\" {\n139|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n140|\t\t\t\t\t}\n141|\t\t\t\t\tcode, detail := \"\", \"\"\n142|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n143|\t\t\t\t\t\tpair, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr)\n144|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n145|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n146|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n147|\t\t\t\t\t\tkey, ok := pair.Key.(*ast.Ident)\n148|\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n149|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n150|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n151|\t\t\t\t\t\tswitch key.Name {\n152|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Code\":\n153|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tsymbol, ok := pair.Value.(*ast.Ident)\n154|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n155|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal code is not a static Code symbol; \"+\n156|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed code cannot be inventoried\", functionName)\n157|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = symbol.Name\n159|\t\t\t\t\t\tcase \"Detail\":\n160|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdetail = staticDetail(t, functionName, pair.Value)\n161|\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n162|\t\t\t\t\t}\n163|\t\t\t\t\tif code == \"\" || detail == \"\" {\n164|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal without a static code and detail; \"+\n165|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"the inventory cannot name what it cannot read\", functionName)\n166|\t\t\t\t\t}\n167|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n168|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n169|\t\t\t\t\t})\n170|\t\t\t\tcase *ast.CallExpr:\n171|\t\t\t\t\tidentifier, ok := expression.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n172|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n173|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n174|\t\t\t\t\t}\n175|\t\t\t\t\tif len(expression.Args) == 0 {\n176|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s without arguments; the derivation cannot name its detail\",\n177|\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName, identifier.Name)\n178|\t\t\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := expression.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n180|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n181|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: %s detail is not a static string literal; \"+\n182|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"a computed detail cannot be inventoried\", functionName, identifier.Name)\n183|\t\t\t\t\t}\n184|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n185|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n186|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", functionName, err)\n187|\t\t\t\t\t}\n188|\t\t\t\t\tcode := \"CodeMismatch\"\n189|\t\t\t\t\tif identifier.Name == \"integrityFailure\" {\n190|\t\t\t\t\t\tcode = \"CodeIntegrityFailure\"\n191|\t\t\t\t\t}\n192|\t\t\t\t\tarms = append(arms, refusalArm{\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\tfile: name, function: functionName, code: code, detail: detail,\n194|\t\t\t\t\t})\n195|\t\t\t\t}\n196|\t\t\t\treturn true\n197|\t\t\t})\n198|\t\t}\n199|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n200|\t\t\tswitch decl := declaration.(type) {\n201|\t\t\tcase *ast.FuncDecl:\n202|\t\t\t\tif decl.Body == nil {\n203|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n204|\t\t\t\t}\n205|\t\t\t\tif constructorFunctions[decl.Name.Name] {\n206|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n207|\t\t\t\t}\n208|\t\t\t\tfunctionName := decl.Name.Name\n209|\t\t\t\tif decl.Recv != nil && len(decl.Recv.List) > 0 {\n210|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = receiverTypeName(decl.Recv.List[0].Type) + \".\" + functionName\n211|\t\t\t\t}\n212|\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, decl.Body)\n213|\t\t\tcase *ast.GenDecl:\n214|\t\t\t\t// Package-level initializers execute outside any FuncDecl,\n215|\t\t\t\t// so a func literal (or a bare &Error{}) assigned to a\n216|\t\t\t\t// package var would otherwise ship invisible. Attribute\n217|\t\t\t\t// its arms to the declared variable name.\n218|\t\t\t\tfor _, spec := range decl.Specs {\n219|\t\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := spec.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n220|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n221|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n222|\t\t\t\t\t}\n223|\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName := \"var\"\n224|\t\t\t\t\tif len(value.Names) > 0 {\n225|\t\t\t\t\t\tfunctionName = value.Names[0].Name\n226|\t\t\t\t\t}\n227|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, item := range value.Values {\n228|\t\t\t\t\t\tcollect(functionName, item)\n229|\t\t\t\t\t}\n230|\t\t\t\t}\n231|\t\t\t}\n232|\t\t}\n233|\t\trejectConstructorAliases(t, file, name)\n234|\t}\n235|\t_ = parsed\n236|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n237|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n238|\t}\n239|\toccurrences := make(map[refusalArm]int)\n240|\tfor index := range arms {\n241|\t\tkey := arms[index]\n242|\t\tkey.occurrence = 0\n243|\t\toccurrences[key]++\n244|\t\tarms[index].occurrence = occurrences[key]\n245|\t}\n246|\treturn arms\n247|}\n248|\n249|// rejectConstructorAliases fails the suite when a refusal constructor\n250|// (mismatchf, integrityFailure) is referenced outside direct-call\n251|// position. `refuse := mismatchf; refuse(\"…\")` ships a reachable arm the\n252|// arm derivation above cannot attribute to a static call site, so the\n253|// reference itself is the violation: call the constructor directly.\n254|// The constructors' own declarations are excluded; their bodies are the\n255|// funnel, not arms. Any other use — alias, argument, field, shadow —\n256|// fails closed, because no legitimate production shape needs it.\n257|func rejectConstructorAliases(t *testing.T, file *ast.File, name string) {\n258|\tt.Helper()\n259|\n260|\tallowed := map[token.Pos]bool{}\n261|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n262|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n263|\t\tif !ok {\n264|\t\t\tif call, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n265|\t\t\t\tif identifier, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident); ok && constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] {\n266|\t\t\t\t\tallowed[identifier.Pos()] = true\n267|\t\t\t\t}\n268|\t\t\t}\n269|\t\t\treturn true\n270|\t\t}\n271|\t\tif constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n272|\t\t\tallowed[declaration.Name.Pos()] = true\n273|\t\t\treturn false\n274|\t\t}\n275|\t\treturn true\n276|\t})\n277|\tast.Inspect(file, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n278|\t\tdeclaration, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n279|\t\tif ok && constructorFunctions[declaration.Name.Name] {\n280|\t\t\treturn false\n281|\t\t}\n282|\t\tidentifier, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n283|\t\tif !ok || !constructorFunctions[identifier.Name] || allowed[identifier.Pos()] {\n284|\t\t\treturn true\n285|\t\t}\n286|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: constructor %q referenced outside direct-call position; \"+\n287|\t\t\t\"an aliased refusal cannot be inventoried, call it directly\", name, identifier.Name)\n288|\t\treturn true\n289|\t})\n290|}\n291|\n292|// receiverTypeName renders a method receiver type to its bare name.\n293|func receiverTypeName(expression ast.Expr) string {\n294|\tswitch typed := expression.(type) {\n295|\tcase *ast.Ident:\n296|\t\treturn typed.Name\n297|\tcase *ast.StarExpr:\n298|\t\treturn receiverTypeName(typed.X)\n299|\tdefault:\n300|\t\treturn \"unknown\"\n301|\t}\n302|}\n303|\n304|// staticDetail reads one Detail expression: a string literal, or the one\n305|// dynamic funnel. Anything else fails the derivation.\n306|func staticDetail(t *testing.T, function string, expression ast.Expr) string {\n307|\tt.Helper()\n308|\n309|\tif literal, ok := expression.(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n310|\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n311|\t\tif err != nil {\n312|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: unquote detail: %v\", function, err)\n313|\t\t}\n314|\t\treturn detail\n315|\t}\n316|\tif call, ok := expression.(*ast.CallExpr); ok {\n317|\t\tif selector, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.SelectorExpr); ok && selector.Sel.Name == \"Error\" {\n318|\t\t\tif receiver, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident); ok && receiver.Name == \"err\" {\n319|\t\t\t\treturn passthroughDetail\n320|\t\t\t}\n321|\t\t}\n322|\t}\n323|\tt.Fatalf(\"%s: refusal Detail is not a static clause; Detail must never \"+\n324|\t\t\"interpolate local data, and a dynamic detail cannot be inventoried\", function)\n325|\treturn \"\"\n326|}\n327|\n328|// productionCodeSymbols resolves every Code symbol to its wire value from\n329|// the production const declarations, so the declared table cannot drift\n330|// from the codes production actually emits.\n331|func productionCodeSymbols(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n332|\tt.Helper()\n333|\n334|\tsymbols := make(map[string]string)\n335|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n336|\tif err != nil {\n337|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n338|\t}\n339|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n340|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n341|\t\t\tcontinue\n342|\t\t}\n343|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n344|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n345|\t\tif err != nil {\n346|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n347|\t\t}\n348|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n349|\t\t\tgeneral, ok := declaration.(*ast.GenDecl)\n350|\t\t\tif !ok || general.Tok != token.CONST {\n351|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n352|\t\t\t}\n353|\t\t\tfor _, specification := range general.Specs {\n354|\t\t\t\tvalue, ok := specification.(*ast.ValueSpec)\n355|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n356|\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n357|\t\t\t\t}\n358|\t\t\t\tfor index, name := range value.Names {\n359|\t\t\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name.Name, \"Code\") || index >= len(value.Values) {\n360|\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n361|\t\t\t\t\t}\n362|\t\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := value.Values[index].(*ast.BasicLit)\n363|\t\t\t\t\tif !ok || literal.Kind != token.STRING {\n364|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"code symbol %s is not a static string; \"+\n365|\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"wire codes must be literals\", name.Name)\n366|\t\t\t\t\t}\n367|\t\t\t\t\twire, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n368|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n369|\t\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unquote %s: %v\", name.Name, err)\n370|\t\t\t\t\t}\n371|\t\t\t\t\tsymbols[name.Name] = wire\n372|\t\t\t\t}\n373|\t\t\t}\n374|\t\t}\n375|\t}\n376|\tif len(symbols) == 0 {\n377|\t\tt.Fatal(\"resolved zero code symbols; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n378|\t}\n379|\treturn symbols\n380|}\n381|\n382|// testBodies indexes every test declaration in this package by file and\n383|// name to its body source. A duplicate test name across files fails: row\n384|// references would be ambiguous.\n385|func testBodies(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n386|\tt.Helper()\n387|\n388|\tbodies := make(map[string]string)\n389|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*_test.go\")\n390|\tif err != nil {\n391|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob test files: %v\", err)\n392|\t}\n393|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n394|\t\tt.Fatal(\"found zero test files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n395|\t}\n396|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n397|\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(name)\n398|\t\tif err != nil {\n399|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read %s: %v\", name, err)\n400|\t\t}\n401|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n402|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n403|\t\tif err != nil {\n404|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n405|\t\t}\n406|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n407|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n408|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Test\") {\n409|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n410|\t\t\t}\n411|\t\t\tstart := fileSet.Position(function.Body.Pos()).Offset\n412|\t\t\tend := fileSet.Position(function.Body.End()).Offset\n413|\t\t\tkey := name + \"\\n\" + function.Name.Name\n414|\t\t\tif _, duplicate := bodies[key]; duplicate {\n415|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"test %s is declared twice; row references would be ambiguous\", key)\n416|\t\t\t}\n417|\t\t\tbodies[key] = string(raw[start:end])\n418|\t\t}\n419|\t}\n420|\tif len(bodies) == 0 {\n421|\t\tt.Fatal(\"indexed zero test declarations, so every row below would resolve vacuously\")\n422|\t}\n423|\treturn bodies\n424|}\n425|\n426|// predicateCodes resolves every Is predicate to the code symbol it\n427|// reports, verifying the shape: a single return of errorCode(err, Code).\n428|// A predicate in any other shape fails: the inventory leans on these to\n429|// resolve code-only assertions, so an unrecognized shape proves nothing.\n430|func predicateCodes(t *testing.T) map[string]string {\n431|\tt.Helper()\n432|\n433|\tpredicates := make(map[string]string)\n434|\tmatches, err := filepath.Glob(\"*.go\")\n435|\tif err != nil {\n436|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"glob production files: %v\", err)\n437|\t}\n438|\tfor _, name := range matches {\n439|\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n440|\t\t\tcontinue\n441|\t\t}\n442|\t\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n443|\t\tfile, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, name, nil, 0)\n444|\t\tif err != nil {\n445|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse %s: %v\", name, err)\n446|\t\t}\n447|\t\tfor _, declaration := range file.Decls {\n448|\t\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n449|\t\t\tif !ok || !strings.HasPrefix(function.Name.Name, \"Is\") || function.Body == nil {\n450|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
