\n484|}\n485|\n486|// declaredRefusalArm is one inventoried arm: the derived key (file,\n487|// function, code symbol, static detail, occurrence), the public\n488|// production entry its test drives, an optional stated bound for\n489|// defensive arms no document can reach, and the tests asserting it.\n490|type declaredRefusalArm struct {\n491|\tfile       string\n492|\tfunction   string\n493|\tcode       string\n494|\tdetail     string\n495|\toccurrence int\n496|\tentry      string\n497|\tbound      string\n498|\t// detailSet carries the funneled detail set for the single\n499|\t// dynamic-detail row; it is empty for every literal row.\n500|\tdetailSet []string\n501|\ttests     []refusalTestRef\n502|}\n503|\n504|// boundDefensiveReparse is the stated bound for re-parse arms after an\n505|// already-validated member: timestampMember validated the member, and the\n506|// Time re-parse cannot fail while scalar owns that contract. The arms\n507|// stay as fail-closed defense; the bound says why no document reaches\n508|// them, and TestDefensiveBoundsAreExactlyThese pins the set.\n509|const boundDefensiveReparse = \"defensive re-parse after validation; scalar owns the re-parse contract\"\n510|\n511|// declaredRefusalArms is the inventoried arm set. Field order is file,\n512|// function (receiver-qualified for methods), code symbol, static detail,\n513|// occurrence within that key, driven public entry, stated bound (empty\n514|// except for defensive arms), funneled detail set (nil except the funnel\n515|// row, which lives outside this table), and asserting tests.\n516|//\n517|// The table is generated from the derivation, never hand-enumerated:\n518|// every row must match exactly one derived arm and vice versa, so adding\n519|// a production arm without a row fails forward, and deleting one fails\n520|// in reverse.\n521|var declaredRefusalArms = []declaredRefusalArm{\n522|\t{\"conformance.go\", \"CheckAttachRequest\", \"CodeMismatch\", \"document timestamp\", 1, \"