{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c841","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06fb4-3612-7082-aba0-c5e534814a47"},"sequence":635,"recorded_at":1780531400001265,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"eabad717-3e00-45d4-b352-a95943b57e50"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7ac7a4aa-20bf-403b-add1-0f0ae94c2216"},"task_id":"7ac7a4aa-20bf-403b-add1-0f0ae94c2216","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"7ac7a4aa-20bf-403b-add1-0f0ae94c2216","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-19-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"cannot ship unwitnessed\\\\|anywhere\\\\|P11\\\\|declined\\\" README.md | head -n 20; echo ===; sed -n '725,745p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check README claims and LOGBOOK bounds\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"===\\n- FINDING: Deriving the refusal arms before writing the inventory found two genuinely unwitnessed arms, not review hypotheticals: `Registry.AdmitProbe` on a nil registry (nil check first, so no fixture needed) and `ParseEvidence` on malformed `observed_at`/`expires_at` (timestamp parse precedes identity recomputation, proven by the new cases passing). Both now have tests. Seven further arms are dead by construction with the bound stated, not inferred: two `evidence canonical bytes` arms (serializes a fixed string/bool/null map; `encoding/json` and JCS cannot fail on it) and five re-parse `document timestamp` arms after an already-validated member (this leaf's three plus `checkEvidenceLiveness`'s two, pinned as exactly these five).\\n- FINDING: The single dynamic-detail funnel is `Registration.validate` wrapping `validatePlatforms` via `err.Error()`. The inventory pins the funneled set exactly (three details, derived from the AST both ways) and allowlists plain-error construction to `validatePlatforms` and `DigestFile` only, with `DigestFile` failures asserted never-`*Error` behaviorally. A second funnel or a new plain-error refusal site is a red.\\n- DECISION: Row resolution is detail-mention OR (entry-mention AND wire-or-verified-predicate-mention), with predicates verified from the production AST. External tests assert codes through predicates with isolating fixtures; demanding detail strings there would misdescribe the battery. Misattribution (right detail, wrong test) remains a review finding — three such rows were caught by reading the generated table, not by the gate.\\n- EVIDENCE: 8 copy-aside mutants, each grep-confirmed present and restored `cmp`-clean: M1 replays the reviewer's exact attack (new arm, new detail) and fails forward naming the arm plus reverse on the count; M2 reuses an existing detail in a new function and fails on the function key; M3/M4/M7 narrow rather than delete and fail at `error = <nil>`; M5 (deleted relay refusal) fails the gate and both inventory directions via the stale row; M6 (swapped legacy map) fails three translation tests; M9 (deleted table row) fails forward plus the bijection. 8/8 killed, 0 survivors.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (new); `manifest_test.go` (+2 evidence-timestamp cases), `terminalbackend_test.go` (+5 wire codes); `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` (+`terminal-lifecycle-conformance` acceptance case, 75->76), `traceability.go` (projection digest), `traceability_test.go`, `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`. Section bindings untouched: still `unevidenced` with honest gaps, no clause-level claims added.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14 packages), `-race` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Package coverage 89.9% statements (reviewer-measured on the rev-1 tree; 90.0% was my rounding error). New files left untracked in the working tree; no commit (board checkpoints). TASK-260830-1snnef handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-1 rework: four sampled closures, closed by derivation\\n- FINDING (F1): The refusal-arm derivation walked FuncDecl bodies only, so a package-level `var f = func() *Error {…}` arm and an aliased constructor (`refuse := mismatchf`) each shipped reachable with a new detail while both inventory tests stayed green. Both shapes measured empty in the tree, so the 193/193 ratio held while the closure claim did not.\\n- FIX (F1, preferred over a caveat): the derivation now scans every FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer (attributed to the variable name), and `rejectConstructorAliases` fatals on any constructor reference outside direct-call position. Replayed both reviewer probes copy-aside with shasum-verified restore: A1 fails the bijection (194 derived vs 193 rows), A2 fatals at the alias. Zero table change — both shapes are still empty in the tree.\\n- FIX (F2): `TestCheckErrorAllowedRefusesEveryUnlistedCode` was a 3–5-code sample named as a complement. It now derives the complement: a full-row mirror table (`allowedErrorCodesByOperation`, all ten rows exact) is proved a subset of production by the exhaustive admit test and production is proved a subset of the mirror over the pinned catalog (`catalog.Current().Errors`) by the refusal loop, with a mirror-inside-catalog pin and fail-closed empty-domain guards. P20 (admit `terminal_backend_unavailable` for all ten ops) now fails the suite. Non-catalog strings are an unbounded domain: three probes pin the shape with the sampling bound stated, not claimed as closure.\\n- FIX (F3): added `CheckAttachResult(false, false, auth{InputAuthorized:true})` — the case only the third conjunct catches. Dropping `resultInputAuthorized != auth.InputAuthorized` now fails the suite.\\n- FIX (F4): attach expiry pinned from both sides — admitted one second before `expires`, refused exactly at it. `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` now fails the suite.\\n- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\\\"operation vocabulary\\\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closures: P11 (legacy escape name over an unbounded string domain) and P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code).\\n- EVIDENCE: A1/A2/P8/P16/P20 replayed, each red with exit 1, tree restored byte-identical (shasum). Full gates re-run below.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (derivation + bounds), `conformance_test.go` (F2–F4); `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry, 89.9% correction). No production change, no table change, README sentence stands as written now that the derivation covers it.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, section coverage unchanged). Package coverage 90.0% statements measured on this rework tree (test-only additions vs the rev-1 tree the reviewer measured at 89.9%). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6424,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1606,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
